WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.280
A rapper, actors and a broadway star.&nbsp;
For one reason or another parted ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.560
from their jobs for refusing to get vaccinated.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:14.400
In November of 2021, "General Hospital" fans were&nbsp;
shocked to discover longtime star Steve Burton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.580
who portrayed Jason Morgan&nbsp;
on the drama for 30 years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.300
had been fired from the series&nbsp;
following his refusal to get the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:27.180
COVID-19 vaccine. The actor said as much&nbsp;
via an Instagram post in which he stated:

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:47.160
Per Deadline, Burton tested&nbsp;
positive for COVID-19 in August,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:52.215
but he explained how his decision not to get&nbsp;
the vaccine came down to personal freedom.

00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:56.250
"I don't think anybody should&nbsp;
lose their livelihood over this."

00:00:56.250 --> 00:01:00.480
Burton doesn't rule out a return to&nbsp;
"General Hospital," although his character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.340
was presumably killed off in an episode that&nbsp;
aired shortly before his Instagram comments.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:10.980
As it turns out, Steve Burton wasn't the only&nbsp;
"General Hospital" star who refused the COVID-19&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:17.460
vaccine. Fellow actor Ingo Rademacher, who had&nbsp;
starred as Jasper Jacks on the series since 1996,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.440
likewise attempted to file a religious exemption,&nbsp;
and was quickly denied, and fired from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:28.740
show. Rolling Stone published the actor's&nbsp;
exemption letter on Dec. 13, 2021. It reads,

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:54.240
The sudden turn of events opened the door for even&nbsp;
more drama when Rademacher filed a lawsuit against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:02:00.420
ABC, as he felt the COVID-19 protocols were a&nbsp;
direct violation of his civil rights. He stated,

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:10.965
The case goes to court in February&nbsp;
2023, according to Radar Online.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.605
Following Ingo Rademacher's lead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.605 --> 00:02:18.840
"9-1-1" star Rockmond Dunbar likewise filed&nbsp;
a lawsuit against Disney and 20th Television&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:23.100
for refusing to honor his request for a&nbsp;
religious exemption regarding the vaccine.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:29.610
"And I said to myself, I can do that too."

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:35.880
After portraying Michael Grant for 69 episodes,&nbsp;
the actor had his contract terminated in November&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:41.940
2021. That followed his refusal to comply&nbsp;
with studio mandates, an action he felt was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:48.420
discriminatory. As such, he attempted to navigate&nbsp;
the situation via religious exemption to no avail,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:54.420
leading Dunbar to sue in February 2022.&nbsp;
The actor said in a statement to Deadline,

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.060
Despite the controversy, Dunbar is scheduled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.660
to appear in upcoming productions&nbsp;
"Red Winter" and "The Waterboyz."

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:23.700
Another name that popped up in the wake of&nbsp;
the COVID-19 vaccine controversy was Andrea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:29.100
Bordeaux. She revealed on Instagram that she&nbsp;
was fired from the Starz-Lionsgate TV series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:35.580
"Run the World" after failing to follow on-set&nbsp;
guidelines. In the post, she discussed how much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:41.460
fun she had working on the production, calling&nbsp;
the experience a "dream come true" and saying that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:47.745
she had no desire to exit the series. Bordeaux&nbsp;
wrote in response to a report posted by Deadline,

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.580
Bordeaux appeared in all eight episodes of Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:04.560
1 of "Run the World" as Ella. She also&nbsp;
had appeared in TV shows such as "NCIS:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.720
Los Angeles," "Criminal Minds" and "Law and&nbsp;
Order: Special Victims Unit." According to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:15.450
her IMDb profile, the actor is not slated&nbsp;
to appear in any upcoming productions.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:20.820
Ice Cube wasn't fired from the production of&nbsp;
the comedy "Oh Hell No," which was set to shoot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:27.060
in winter 2021, but he exited the film after&nbsp;
turning down the COVID-19 vaccine, according&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:33.840
to The Hollywood Reporter. As a result of his&nbsp;
exit, Ice Cube lost out on a $9 million payday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:37.500
If he had stayed on, the movie&nbsp;
would have paired him alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.880
the great Jack Black and Netflix's&nbsp;
"Bad Trip" director, Kitao Sakurai.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:47.700
Even still, the popular rapper-actor was&nbsp;
a vocal supporter of mask-wearing and even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:51.840
helped support the cause by selling T-shirts&nbsp;
inscribed with the phrase "Check Yo Self&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:56.760
Before You Wreck Yo Self." Ice Cube also&nbsp;
ended up departing a Universal Pictures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:01.800
project called "Flint Strong," which actually&nbsp;
filmed for one day before production was put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:07.740
on hiatus in March 2020 as the spread of&nbsp;
COVID began to accelerate. It's not clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:12.690
why he left that film, which is said to be&nbsp;
looking for a new star and possibly studio.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:16.020
As of now, no one has been tapped to replace Ice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:20.220
Cube in "Oh Hell No," though Jack&nbsp;
Black is currently still aboard.

